1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,210
Man:

2
00:00:02,210 --> 00:00:02,894
Excuse me.

3
00:00:02,894 --> 00:00:05,381
Would you mind if I asked you some questions?

4
00:00:05,381 --> 00:00:08,520
We’re doing a survey on transport.

5
00:00:08,520 --> 00:00:08,960
Sadie:

6
00:00:08,960 --> 00:00:09,400
Yes,

7
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:10,720
that’s OK.

8
00:00:10,720 --> 00:00:11,024
Man:

9
00:00:11,024 --> 00:00:13,460
First of all, can I take your name?

10
00:00:13,460 --> 00:00:13,967
Sadie:

11
00:00:13,967 --> 00:00:14,473
Yes.

12
00:00:14,473 --> 00:00:16,500
It’s Sadie Jones.

13
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:16,819
Man:

14
00:00:16,819 --> 00:00:17,776
Thanks very much.

15
00:00:17,776 --> 00:00:22,244
And could I have your date of birth – just the year will do, actually.

16
00:00:22,244 --> 00:00:23,520
Is that all right?

17
00:00:23,520 --> 00:00:24,155
Sadie:

18
00:00:24,155 --> 00:00:24,790
Yes,

19
00:00:24,790 --> 00:00:26,695
that’s fine.

20
00:00:26,695 --> 00:00:28,600
It’s 1991.

21
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:29,188
Man:

22
00:00:29,188 --> 00:00:32,130
So next your postcode, please.

23
00:00:32,130 --> 00:00:33,344
Sadie:

24
00:00:33,344 --> 00:00:38,200
It’s DW30 7YZ.

25
00:00:38,200 --> 00:00:38,737
Man:

26
00:00:38,737 --> 00:00:39,274
Great.

27
00:00:39,274 --> 00:00:39,811
Thanks.

28
00:00:39,811 --> 00:00:41,960
Is that in Wells?

29
00:00:41,960 --> 00:00:42,340
Sadie:

30
00:00:42,340 --> 00:00:47,280
No it’s actually in Harborne – Wells isn’t far from there, though.

31
00:00:47,280 --> 00:00:47,601
Man:

32
00:00:47,601 --> 00:00:49,208
I really like that area.

33
00:00:49,208 --> 00:00:52,100
My grandmother lived there when I was a kid.

34
00:00:52,100 --> 00:00:52,558
Sadie:

35
00:00:52,558 --> 00:00:54,390
Yes, it is nice.

36
00:00:54,390 --> 00:00:54,791
Man:

37
00:00:54,791 --> 00:00:55,193
Right,

38
00:00:55,193 --> 00:01:00,812
so now I want to ask you some questions about how you travelled here

39
00:01:00,812 --> 00:01:01,213
today.

40
00:01:01,213 --> 00:01:03,220
Did you use public transport?

41
00:01:03,220 --> 00:01:03,627
Sadie:

42
00:01:03,627 --> 00:01:04,033
Yes.

43
00:01:04,033 --> 00:01:05,660
I came by bus.

44
00:01:05,660 --> 00:01:06,057
Man:

45
00:01:06,057 --> 00:01:06,453
OK.

46
00:01:06,453 --> 00:01:08,040
And that was today.

47
00:01:08,040 --> 00:01:11,610
It’s the 24th of April, isn’t it?

48
00:01:11,610 --> 00:01:12,229
Sadie:

49
00:01:12,229 --> 00:01:15,325
Isn’t it the 25th?

50
00:01:15,325 --> 00:01:18,420
No, actually, you’re right.

51
00:01:18,420 --> 00:01:18,706
Man:

52
00:01:18,706 --> 00:01:21,275
And what was the reason for your trip today?

53
00:01:21,275 --> 00:01:24,130
I can see you’ve got some shopping with you.

54
00:01:24,130 --> 00:01:24,527
Sadie:

55
00:01:24,527 --> 00:01:24,925
Yes.

56
00:01:24,925 --> 00:01:30,488
I did some shopping but the main reason I came here was to go

57
00:01:30,488 --> 00:01:31,680
to the dentist.

58
00:01:31,680 --> 00:01:32,005
Man:

59
00:01:32,005 --> 00:01:33,627
That’s not much fun.

60
00:01:33,627 --> 00:01:35,250
Hope it was nothing serious.

61
00:01:35,250 --> 00:01:35,586
Sadie:

62
00:01:35,586 --> 00:01:37,602
No, it was just a check-up.

63
00:01:37,602 --> 00:01:38,610
It’s fine.

64
00:01:38,610 --> 00:01:38,980
Man:

65
00:01:38,980 --> 00:01:39,350
Good.

66
00:01:39,350 --> 00:01:43,050
Do you normally travel by bus into the city centre?

67
00:01:43,050 --> 00:01:43,510
Sadie:

68
00:01:43,510 --> 00:01:43,971
Yes.

69
00:01:43,971 --> 00:01:49,958
I stopped driving in ages ago because parking was so difficult to find

70
00:01:49,958 --> 00:01:52,260
and it costs so much.

71
00:01:52,260 --> 00:01:52,633
Man:

72
00:01:52,633 --> 00:01:53,380
I see.

73
00:01:53,380 --> 00:01:53,771
Sadie:

74
00:01:53,771 --> 00:01:56,511
The bus is much more convenient too.

75
00:01:56,511 --> 00:01:58,860
It only takes about 30 minutes.

76
00:01:58,860 --> 00:01:59,202
Man:

77
00:01:59,202 --> 00:02:00,227
That’s good.

78
00:02:00,227 --> 00:02:02,620
So where did you start your journey?

79
00:02:02,620 --> 00:02:03,090
Sadie:

80
00:02:03,090 --> 00:02:06,380
At the bus stop on Claxby Street.

81
00:02:06,380 --> 00:02:07,262
Man:

82
00:02:07,262 --> 00:02:10,790
Is that C-L-A–X-B-Y?

83
00:02:10,790 --> 00:02:11,842
Sadie:

84
00:02:11,842 --> 00:02:15,000
That’s right.

85
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:15,329
Man:

86
00:02:15,329 --> 00:02:17,964
And how satisfied with the service are you?

87
00:02:17,964 --> 00:02:19,610
Do you have any complaints?

88
00:02:19,610 --> 00:02:20,032
Sadie:

89
00:02:20,032 --> 00:02:25,942
Well, as I said, it’s very convenient and quick when it’s on

90
00:02:25,942 --> 00:02:26,364
time,

91
00:02:26,364 --> 00:02:28,897
but this morning it was late.

92
00:02:28,897 --> 00:02:30,586
Only about 10 minutes,

93
00:02:30,586 --> 00:02:31,430
but still.

94
00:02:31,430 --> 00:02:31,781
Man:

95
00:02:31,781 --> 00:02:33,887
Yes, I understand that’s annoying.

96
00:02:33,887 --> 00:02:35,643
And what about the timetable?

97
00:02:35,643 --> 00:02:38,100
Do you have any comments about that?

98
00:02:38,100 --> 00:02:38,489
Sadie:

99
00:02:38,489 --> 00:02:38,878
Mmm.

100
00:02:38,878 --> 00:02:42,767
I suppose I mainly use the bus during the day,

101
00:02:42,767 --> 00:02:47,823
but any time I’ve been in town in the evening – for dinner

102
00:02:47,823 --> 00:02:53,269
or at the cinema – I’ve noticed you have to wait a long time

103
00:02:53,269 --> 00:02:56,380
for a bus – there aren’t that many.

104
00:02:56,380 --> 00:02:56,763
Man:

105
00:02:56,763 --> 00:02:57,528
OK, thanks.

106
00:02:57,528 --> 00:03:02,120
So now I’d like to ask you about your car use.

107
00:03:02,120 --> 00:03:02,477
Sadie:

108
00:03:02,477 --> 00:03:07,480
Well, I have got a car but I don’t use it that often.

109
00:03:07,480 --> 00:03:09,981
Mainly just to go to the supermarket.

110
00:03:09,981 --> 00:03:12,125
But that’s about it really.

111
00:03:12,125 --> 00:03:16,770
My husband uses it at the weekends to go to the golf club.

112
00:03:16,770 --> 00:03:17,070
Man:

113
00:03:17,070 --> 00:03:18,570
And what about a bicycle?

114
00:03:18,570 --> 00:03:18,836
Sadie:

115
00:03:18,836 --> 00:03:21,230
I don’t actually have one at the moment.

116
00:03:21,230 --> 00:03:21,519
Man:

117
00:03:21,519 --> 00:03:23,827
What about the city bikes you can rent?

118
00:03:23,827 --> 00:03:25,270
Do you ever use those?

119
00:03:25,270 --> 00:03:25,594
Sadie:

120
00:03:25,594 --> 00:03:29,805
No – I’m not keen on cycling there because of all the pollution.

121
00:03:29,805 --> 00:03:34,016
But I would like to get a bike – it would be good to

122
00:03:34,016 --> 00:03:35,960
use it to get to work.

123
00:03:35,960 --> 00:03:36,232
Man:

124
00:03:36,232 --> 00:03:38,410
So why haven’t you got one now?

125
00:03:38,410 --> 00:03:38,766
Sadie:

126
00:03:38,766 --> 00:03:42,327
Well, I live in a flat – on the second floor

127
00:03:42,327 --> 00:03:47,669
and it doesn’t have any storage – so we’d have to leave it in

128
00:03:47,669 --> 00:03:49,450
the hall outside the flat.

129
00:03:49,450 --> 00:03:49,810
Man:

130
00:03:49,810 --> 00:03:50,530
I see.

131
00:03:50,530 --> 00:03:50,890
OK.

132
00:03:50,890 --> 00:03:53,050
Well, I think that’s all ...
